From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 09:49:09 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] d3d11, dxgi, win32u: textures shared between processes on
 D3DKMT resources, OpenSharedResource1 and ByName, IDXGIResource1 (3324)

CORE review: graphics. Textures made with D3D11_RESOURCE_MISC_SHARED,
SHARED_KEYEDMUTEX and SHARED_NTHANDLE were shared between the devices of one
process only (a list in d3d11, fake handles). They are D3DKMT resources now
(3321-3323): the texture's description is the private runtime data of a shared
resource, its pixels the content of the allocation, its keyed mutex a D3DKMT
keyed mutex. So another process opens them: ID3D11Device::OpenSharedResource
and ID3D10Device::OpenSharedResource with the legacy handle of
IDXGIResource::GetSharedHandle, ID3D11Device1::OpenSharedResource1 with an NT
handle from the new IDXGIResource1::CreateSharedHandle (inheritable, or
named), OpenSharedResourceByName, and IDXGIFactory2::GetSharedResourceAdapterLuid
for both kinds of handle.

AcquireSync/ReleaseSync order the processes with the keys and hand the pixels
over with them (ReleaseSync copies the texture to the content, AcquireSync takes
what is new); a mutex whose holder exits or whose texture is destroyed is
abandoned. A texture without a mutex hands its pixels over when its device is
flushed and somebody has it open, and the opener takes them when its device is
flushed (and at once, from a texture of its own process, when it opens).

win32u: the access of a handle from ShareObjects always allows mapping the
block (DXGI_SHARED_RESOURCE_READ/WRITE are generic bits). include/wine/kmtshare.h
lists in include/Makefile.in so PE modules can include it; it also has the header
the Direct3D runtime's private runtime data starts with (DXGI reads the adapter
there).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01XZFS4SPPzeH5d2c1MuzqCS


Rebased at integration (integ-2026-10) onto 3719/3726/3730 (fast-b): 3324 replaces the in-process shared textures with D3DKMT resources, so fast-b 3719's d3d11 private export wine_d3d11_get_shared_resource_adapter_luid (and its spec line) and the old d3d_shared_resource list go; IDXGIFactory2::GetSharedResourceAdapterLuid uses 3324's dxgi_shared_resource_luid for both handle kinds.
